          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A relevant monad is a special kind of monad which is related to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relevance+logic"} relevance logic
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T, \mu,\eta)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            Recall that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is said to be
            %strong right-strong
            with respect to the Cartesian product (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} strong monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_{X,Y} : T(X)\times Y\to T(X\times Y)
            satisfying some coherence conditions which can be found on the linked page.
          %p
            In what follows, fix a monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T, \mu,\eta)
            together with a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strength"} right strength
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            for the Cartesian product.
          %p
            Using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetry isomorphism
            of the Cartesian product it is possible to give a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strength"} left strength
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha'_{A,B} : A\times T(B)\to T(A\times B)
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A\times T(B) \cong T(B)\times A \xrightarrow{\alpha_{B,A}}T(B\times A)\cong T(A\times B)
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Let
