          %p
          %h2#section_References References
          %p Concept was first introduced here, see Prop 2.2:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
              ,
              %em Bilinearity and Cartesian-Closed Monads
              In: Mathematica Scandinavica 29.2 (1971), pp. 161–74.
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/24491025"} JSTOR: 24491025
              %a{:href => "https://users-math.au.dk/kock/BCCM.pdf"} pdf
          %p Jacobs is probably the first one to introduce the name ‘relevant monad’:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bart+Jacobs"}> Bart Jacobs
              ,
              %em Semantics of Weakening and Contraction
              In: Annals of
              %p
                Pure and Applied Logic 69.1 (Sept. 1994), pp. 73–106. issn: 01680072.
                %a{:href => "https://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/0168007294900205"} doi: 10.1016/0168-0072(94)90020-5
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Louis Parlant et al.,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Preservation of Equations by Monoidal Monads
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/2001.06348"} arXiv: 2001.06348 [cs, math]
